  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Connecticut has $18.3B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The number of awards totals 23,423 and the average award size is $781K. Obligations are down 48.0% year over year. Fiscal history shows variation: FY21 obligations were $18.4B, FY22 obligations were $22.3B, FY23 obligations were $26B, FY24 obligations were $20B, and FY25 obligations were $35.1B. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $17.9B so far in FY2026. Engineering Services is the largest industry by obligations with $6.9B, followed by Ship Building and Repairing with $3.9B and Aircraft Manufacturing with $3.2B. ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION leads vendors with $10.8B in obligations, followed by RTX CORPORATION with $3.7B and SIKORSKY AIRCRAFT CORPORATION with $2.8B. This snapshot covers partial current-year totals and reflects contract obligations recorded through the fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in Connecticut federal contracting this year?",
        "body": "Connecticut has $18.3B in FY2026 to date obligations, down 48.0% year over year. The award count is 23,423 and the average award size is $781K. Year-to-year totals show large swings from FY21 through FY25, peaking at $35.1B in FY25 before the current-year level."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers and industries in Connecticut?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $17.9B in FY2026 to date, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $110M and the Department of Homeland Security with $108M. Engineering Services leads industries with $6.9B, Ship Building and Repairing follows with $3.9B, and Aircraft Manufacturing has $3.2B in obligations. ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION is the top vendor with $10.8B, followed by RTX CORPORATION with $3.7B and SIKORSKY AIRCRAFT CORPORATION with $2.8B."
      }
    ]
  },
